From 337dc8c8ce392420aa838a30181576fed254280d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gordon Woodhull <gordon.woodhull@posit.co>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:26:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] hub-client: use cross-env for inline env vars in npm scripts
 (Windows)

npm runs scripts through cmd.exe on Windows, which cannot parse the POSIX
`VAR=value command` form, so `npm run build:preview-embed` (and so
`cargo xtask build-hub-client-embed`) failed with "'BUILD_TARGET' is not
recognized as an internal or external command".

Prefix the inline-env commands with cross-env in the three scripts that
sit on the build:all / preview-embed path:

  - hub-client: build, build:preview-embed
  - quarto-hub-sandboxed-preview: build:sw

quarto-hub-sandboxed-preview is not an npm workspace member (its own
package-lock.json, installed by build:sandboxed), so it gets its own
devDependency. Scripts left on the POSIX form: test:e2e, test:e2e:author-id,
test:e2e:ui, test:harness (not exercised here).

Verified on Windows 11: build:sw, build, build:all, and
`cargo xtask build-hub-client-embed` all exit 0; the embed output has the
/ws sync default baked in, no sw.js, no pandoc/, and no Google client id.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
